# Email Sequence: Webinar Registration
# Confirmation + Reminder Emails (sent to registrants)

Use this framework to write the emails that go to people who have already registered for a
webinar/workshop — confirming their spot and reminding them to show up.

---

## Email 1 — Confirmation (send immediately on registration)
Subject: Your Registration for [Webinar Topic] is Confirmed!

Template:
Hello [First Name],

Thank you for registering for my upcoming webinar, [Webinar Topic].

On this webinar, you'll be learning:
- Benefit 1
- Benefit 2
- Benefit 3

I can't wait to share these insights with you.

Below are the details for you to include in your calendar:
Date: [Webinar Date]
Time: [Webinar Time]
Zoom link: [insert link]

I'll send you some reminders a bit closer to the time, but for now — mark the date and time in your diary.

[Signoff]

---

## Email 2 — Reminder (send the day before)
Subject: [Webinar Topic] is tomorrow!

Aim: Jog their memory, remind them of the benefit, incentivise joining live.

Template:
Hello [First Name],

Just a friendly reminder that our webinar, [Webinar Topic], is happening tomorrow at [Webinar Time].

Here's the link to join: [Webinar Link]

On the webinar you're going to learn [big outcome/transformation], and I'll also be answering questions live on the call.

But if you can't make it, don't stress — I'll also be sending out a replay.

See you there!
[Signoff]

PS There will be an exclusive gift for live attendees, so if you CAN make it live, I'd love to see you there.

---

## Email 3 — Last-Minute Reminder (send a few hours before)
Subject: [Webinar Topic] Starts in a Few Hours!

Aim: Final nudge, overview of format, incentivise joining live.

Template:
Hello [First Name],

Our webinar, [Webinar Topic], is starting in a few hours! Here are the details:

Time: [Webinar Time]
Link to join: [insert link]

I'll be spending around 30 minutes teaching you [topic/insight], and then I've put aside around 30 minutes to answer any questions that you might have.

There's also an exclusive gift for those that make the live call, so if you can make it live, I've got something special for you.

But if you can't make it, don't worry — I'll send you the replay.

See you there!
[Signoff]

---

## Email 4 — Post-Webinar Thank You (send after the event)
Subject: [come up with a creative subject line]

Aim: Share the replay, remind them of key insights, hint at upcoming offer.

Template:
Hello [First Name],

Thank you so much for attending [Webinar Topic]. I hope you found it valuable!

There were so many a-ha moments live on the call — I loved delivering [the outcome].

As promised, here's your recording: [link to recording]

Let me know if you have any questions or comments — I'd love to hear from you!

[Signoff]

PS I've got an exclusive offer available for those who registered for the webinar — keep an eye on your inbox for the details!
